    "text": "AdvertisementAdvertisementAdvertisementAdvertisementPowered byTigres hold off Seattle in thriller; Toluca send LA Galaxy packingOneFootballWed, April 15, 2026 at 9:59 p.m. CDT·1 min readAdd Yahoo Sports on GoogleWe met our final two semi-finalists this evening in the Concacaf Champions Cup as LAFC and Nashville await their opponents.Here is what went down.Seattle Sounders 3-1 TigresTigres held on to advance on away goals after a thrilling second leg in Seattle.AdvertisementAdvertisementAdvertisementThe hosts piled the pressure on after pulling to within one on aggregate, but Tigres held on in the face of the relentless Seattle attacks.A Juaquim headed effort in the first-half was the difference in the tie, giving the Liga MX outfit the crucial away goal.After the gutsy win in the Pacific Northwest, Tigres will move on to face Nashville in the semi-finals.LA Galaxy 0-3 TolucaReigning Liga MX champions Toluca comfortably knocked off MLS giants LA Galaxy with a staggering 7-2 aggregate win.AdvertisementAdvertisementAdvertisementThe Galaxy came into the night hoping for a comeback after scoring two away goals south of the border last week, but those hopes were swiftly axed when Jesús Gallardo unleashed a rocket from outside of the box to extend Toluca's lead.A second half brace from veteran striker Paulinho hammered home the advantage for the visitors, seeing them stroll their way into a semi-final matchup with LAFC.AdvertisementTerms and Privacy PolicyPrivacy DashboardAbout Our AdsAdvertisementAdvertisement",
